{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["And you shall double the sixth curtain — that is: half of it hangs below, toward the front of the tent, and half of the last curtain hangs over the back of the Mishkan two cubits more than the curtains of the Mishkan. How so? The ten lower ones, when joined together, are forty cubits long and twenty-eight wide. And the Mishkan is thirty cubits long, for the twenty planks on the north side and the twenty on the south side make thirty cubits, since the width of a plank is a cubit and a half; when spread over the Mishkan, their length along the length of the Mishkan is thirty cubits, and so ten cubits hang behind the Mishkan. And on the north side and on the south side, of the twenty-eight cubits, ten are over the Mishkan and nine hang on each side — nine on the north wall and nine on the south wall. And when one spreads over it the goat-hair curtains, which are forty-four cubits long, half the curtain — that is, two cubits — is doubled below, and thirty over the Mishkan, level with the lower curtains, and twelve remaining: ten of them hang behind the Mishkan level with the lower curtains, plus half the extra curtain, that is, two cubits more than the lower ones. And when one spreads its width, which is thirty cubits after they are joined, then over the width of the Mishkan there are ten cubits of them, and ten cubits hang toward the north and likewise toward the south, so that they extend one cubit on this side and one cubit on that side beyond the lower ones, since those trail nine on each side while these are ten. And this is what is written: והאמה מזה והאמה מזה."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The lemma cites Exodus 26:9. The comment works through the geometry of the tapestry and goat-hair coverings; 'lower ones' (תחתונות) refers to the linen curtains of the Mishkan proper, over which the goat-hair tent-curtains are draped. I have preserved Rashbam's present-tense procedural style throughout."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:15.321197570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}